.TH OOBED 8 "September 2026" "Peios" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
oobed \- Peios first-boot setup service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oobed
.RB [ --socket " " PATH ]
.RB [ --dry-run ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oobed
owns the privileged first-boot conversation.  It creates the first
administrator account, records the machine name in the registry, and retires
its own service definitions only after setup completes.
.PP
The terminal presentation is provided by
.BR oobe-tui (1)
so that user-interface code does not own account or registry privilege.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --socket " PATH"
Listen on PATH instead of
.IR /run/oobed.sock .
.TP
.B --dry-run
Exercise the setup conversation without changing the machine.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show command help.
.TP
.BR -V , " --version"
Show the program version.
.SH SECURITY
The service runs as SYSTEM and accepts MSIP connections only from SYSTEM and
Administrators.  Passwords are sent to
.B lps
over standard input, never as process arguments, and are not written to the
MSIP log.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/oobed.sock
Default MSIP socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR oobe-tui (1),
.BR lps (1),
.BR reg (1)
